### Configure ignorePatterns in Oxlint configuration

Source: https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/ignore-files

Define file exclusion patterns using the recommended ignorePatterns property in either JSON or TypeScript configuration files. Patterns are resolved relative to the configuration file location.

```json
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/oxlint/configuration_schema.json",
  "ignorePatterns": ["dist/**", "coverage/**", "vendor/**", "test/snapshots/**"]
}
```

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from "oxlint";

export default defineConfig({
  ignorePatterns: ["dist/**", "coverage/**", "vendor/**", "test/snapshots/**"],
});
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Oxlint file ignore patterns

Source: https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/quickstart

Configures Oxlint to ignore specific files or patterns. This includes using an explicit ignore file, adding patterns from the command line, and disabling ignore handling.

```shell
oxlint --ignore-path .oxlintignore
```

```shell
oxlint --ignore-pattern "dist/**" --ignore-pattern "*.min.js"
```

```shell
oxlint --no-ignore
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Oxfmt Ignore Patterns

Source: https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/formatter/ignore-files

Specify files and directories to be ignored by Oxfmt using the 'ignorePatterns' key in the .oxfmtrc.json configuration file. This method uses .gitignore syntax and is independent of Git. Paths are relative to the config file's location. Files matching these patterns cannot be formatted.

```json
{
  "ignorePatterns": ["dist/**", "*.min.js"]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Oxlint Configuration File Examples

Source: https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/config-file-reference

Examples of Oxlint configuration files in both JSON (.oxlintrc.json) and TypeScript (.oxlint.config.ts) formats.

```APIDOC
## Oxlint Configuration File Examples

This configuration is aligned with ESLint v8's configuration schema (`eslintrc.json`).

Usage: `oxlint -c oxlintrc.json`

### .oxlintrc.json Example

```json
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/oxlint/configuration_schema.json",
  "plugins": ["import", "typescript", "unicorn"],
  "env": {
    "browser": true
  },
  "globals": {
    "foo": "readonly"
  },
  "settings": {
    "react": {
      "version": "18.2.0"
    },
    "custom": {
      "option": true
    }
  },
  "rules": {
    "eqeqeq": "warn",
    "import/no-cycle": "error",
    "react/self-closing-comp": [
      "error",
      {
        "html": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "overrides": [
    {
      "files": ["*.test.ts", "*.spec.ts"],
      "rules": {
        "@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any": "off"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

### oxlint.config.ts Example

```ts
import { defineConfig } from "oxlint";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: ["import", "typescript", "unicorn"],
  env: {
    browser: true,
  },
  globals: {
    foo: "readonly",
  },
  settings: {
    react: {
      version: "18.2.0",
    },
    custom: { option: true },
  },
  rules: {
    eqeqeq: "warn",
    "import/no-cycle": "error",
    "react/self-closing-comp": ["error", { html: false }],
  },
  overrides: [
    {
      files: ["*.test.ts", "*.spec.ts"],
      rules: {
        "@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any": "off",
      },
    },
  ],
});
```
```

### Ignore files

Source: https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/ignore-files

Large repositories contain files that should not be linted, such as build output, vendored code, snapshots, or generated artifacts. Oxlint provides a predictable ignore model that works well in monorepos and CI.

It is strongly recommended to use `"ignorePatterns"` in your Oxlint config file (`.oxlintrc.json` or `oxlint.config.ts`) for ignoring files rather than a separate ignore file. This ensures that every developer will have the same ignores across all tools and commands running Oxlint, especially IDE/editor integrations. It also keeps your configuration centralized to one file.

